From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PRO 5 Recovery Bring-up <pro5-port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 03:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: force gadget VBUS session when android_usb is enabled

Recovery consistently sees the FUSB302 in the unattached state even with a
USB host connected.  The charger path detects VBUS, but the MUIC notifier
never sends USB_HOST_ATTACH.  android_usb therefore leaves DWC3 outside its
device session and the host cannot enumerate any descriptor.

Treat userspace enabling the configured gadget as sufficient intent to turn
on the DWC3 gadget session.  Keep the normal notifier path in place for later
attach and detach events.
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/android.c | 16 ++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/android.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/android.c
index 63ca6374..311b6e24 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/android.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/android.c
@@ -1495,10 +1495,18 @@ static ssize_t enable_store(struct device *pdev, struct device_attribute *attr,
 				f->enable(f);
 		}
 
-		if (dev->usb_attach) {
-			wake_lock(&dev->wakelock);
-			dwc3_exynos_vbus_event(NULL, 1);
-		}
+		/*
+		 * Recovery can classify an attached USB host as a charger before
+		 * the MUIC notifier reports USB_HOST_ATTACH.  In that case
+		 * usb_attach remains false and DWC3 never enters its gadget
+		 * session, so the host cannot enumerate even an ADB-only setup.
+		 * Userspace enabling android_usb is sufficient intent to prepare
+		 * the device side; a later notifier event remains harmless.
+		 */
+		wake_lock(&dev->wakelock);
+		if (!dev->usb_attach)
+			pr_info("android_usb: forcing DWC3 gadget VBUS session\n");
+		dwc3_exynos_vbus_event(NULL, 1);
 
 		android_enable(dev);
 		dev->enabled = true;
-- 
